# Backend's docker build context is the repo root (see render.yaml's
# dockerContext — needed so the Dockerfile can COPY the sibling Fixtures/
# directory into the image, see Backend/plan.md's B11). Without this file,
# every build would upload the whole monorepo — Frontend's node_modules,
# Backend's own .venv, the iOS App/ project, git history, and any
# .claude/worktrees/* (each a full nested checkout) — instead of just what
# the Dockerfile actually COPYs.

*

!Backend
!Fixtures

Backend/.venv
Backend/__pycache__
Backend/**/__pycache__
Backend/data
Backend/.env
Backend/.neon

# Not needed in the image — the render pipeline uses its own vendored
# soundfont at Backend/app/rendering/resources/TimGM6mb.sf2; this copy is
# for the Frontend/iOS dev fixtures only.
Fixtures/soundfont
Fixtures/**/.DS_Store
